<span id="Sx1.T7.7.30.12.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="Sx1.T7.7.30.12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">13.86</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T7.7.30.13" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:0.8pt;padding-right:0.8pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T7.7.30.13.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="Sx1.T7.7.30.13.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="Sx1.T7.7.30.13.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">86.17</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T7.7.30.14" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:0.8pt;padding-right:0.8pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T7.7.30.14.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="Sx1.T7.7.30.14.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="Sx1.T7.7.30.14.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">86.17</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Runtime Analysis</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our Child-Boxes Diffusion takes 0.33 seconds per split, and  <span id="Sx1.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BoxSplitGen</span> (1.8s) introduces marginal increase over 3DShape2VecSet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">89</a>]</cite> (1.1s), ensuring an efficient, responsive design workflow. All measurements were taken on an RTX 3090 GPU using a <math id="Sx1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>128</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> resolution for Marching Cubes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>Details on User-Interactive Generation Demo</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our demonstration consists of two main components: a web-based viewer and an inference server. The viewer, implemented based on Three.js <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">76</a>]</cite> and Potree <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite>, provides an intuitive interface to manipulate bounding boxes and generate 3D shapes directly in the web browser. The inference server processes API requests and serves results from three pre-trained models: the Pivot Classifier, Child-Boxes Diffusion, and <span id="Sx1.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Box2Shape</span>. Guided by the Pivot Classifier, the viewer identifies the most suitable bounding box to split, and the Child-Boxes Diffusion subsequently performs the actual splitting. Finally, the resulting bounding boxes are used to generate complete 3D shapes via <span id="Sx1.SS8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Box2Shape</span>, whose predicted occupancy fields are converted into 3D meshes using Occupancy-Based Dual Contouring <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>. This integrated workflow enables an interactive and efficient approach to bounding box manipulation and high-fidelity 3D shape generation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>More Quantitative Results of Box Splitting</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present more quantitative results of box splitting generation, as discussed in Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Experiment Results ‣ BoxSplitGen: A Generative Model for 3D Part Bounding Boxes in Varying Granularity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> .
Table <a href="#Sx1.T5" title="Table A5 ‣ Pivot Classifier. ‣ A.6 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix ‣ BoxSplitGen: A Generative Model for 3D Part Bounding Boxes in Varying Granularity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A5</span></a> shows the average results across two split levels, <math id="Sx1.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=8</annotation></semantics></math>, for all eight categories. Meanwhile, Tables <a href="#Sx1.T6" title="Table A6 ‣ Pivot Classifier. ‣ A.6 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix ‣ BoxSplitGen: A Generative Model for 3D Part Bounding Boxes in Varying Granularity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A6</span></a> and <a href="#Sx1.T7" title="Table A7 ‣ Pivot Classifier. ‣ A.6 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix ‣ BoxSplitGen: A Generative Model for 3D Part Bounding Boxes in Varying Granularity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A7</span></a> provide the results for <math id="Sx1.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=8</annotation></semantics></math> separately, using the pivot classifier or random pivot selection, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.10 </span>Qualitative Results of Split Sequence</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#Sx1.F7" title="Figure A7 ‣ A.10 Qualitative Results of Split Sequence ‣ Appendix ‣ BoxSplitGen: A Generative Model for 3D Part Bounding Boxes in Varying Granularity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A7</span></a> shows the evolution of bounding box splitting by our method over multiple splits. Starting from an initial unit cube, the boxes are gradually split to capture finer details, transitioning from a coarse and simple structure to a more refined and complex 3D form. See the first and last rows of Figure <a href="#Sx1.F7" title="Figure A7 ‣ A.10 Qualitative Results of Split Sequence ‣ Appendix ‣ BoxSplitGen: A Generative Model for 3D Part Bounding Boxes in Varying Granularity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A7</span></a> that gradually produce the detail of the lamp shade and the airplane tail, respectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx1.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20666v1/figures/split-sequence/lamp/imgs/0/422.png" id="Sx1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/69;" width="685" height="69" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20666v1/figures/split-sequence/bench/imgs/0/153.png" id="Sx1.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/69;" width="685" height="69" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20666v1/figures/split-sequence/couch/imgs/0/113.png" id="Sx1.F7.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/69;" width="685" height="69" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20666v1/figures/split-sequence/chair/imgs/0/192.png" id="Sx1.F7.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/69;" width="685" height="69" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20666v1/figures/split-sequence/rifle/imgs/0/21.png" id="Sx1.F7.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/69;" width="685" height="69" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20666v1/figures/split-sequence/table/imgs/0/186.png" id="Sx1.F7.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/69;" width="685" height="69" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2602.20666v1/figures/split-sequence/airplane/imgs/0/36.png" id="Sx1.F7.g7" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/69;" width="685" height="69" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx1.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A7</span>: </span><span id="Sx1.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">The evolution of box splits by ours.<span id="Sx1.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In each abstraction, new generated boxes are marked in red, and the pivot to be split in the next split is in blue.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Sx1.SS10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS10.p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="Sx1.SS10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sections for more qualitative results are
<br class="ltx_break">in the following pages.</span></p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
